{% comment %} Comprehensive Testing Section {% endcomment %}
<section class="comprehensive-testing">
  <div class="comprehensive-testing__inner">
    <div class="comprehensive-testing__content">
      <p class="comprehensive-testing__number gh-font-primary h1">02.</p>
      <h2 class="comprehensive-testing__title h1">Comprehensive Testing</h2>
      <h3 class="comprehensive-testing__subtitle">We check everyone’s work so that you can trust ours.</h3>
      <p class="comprehensive-testing__body gh-font-secondary">
        Every shipment of ingredients includes a Certificate of Analysis (COA) that shows the vendor tested for
        identity, purity, safety, and potency (if applicable). But we never rely on that alone. We confirm their
        accuracy through in-house and third-party testing. Any discrepancies suggest that the ingredients were
        adulterated or contaminated. In those cases, we reject the entire batch and seek another source.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="comprehensive-testing__stats">
      <div class="comprehensive-testing__stat">
        <h3 class="comprehensive-testing__stat-value">Around $1M</h3>
        <p class="comprehensive-testing__stat-label gh-font-secondary">
          spent on testing per year*
          <span class="comprehensive-testing__stat-note">(*based on 2025)</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="comprehensive-testing__stat">
        <h3 class="comprehensive-testing__stat-value">Multiple Rounds</h3>
        <p class="comprehensive-testing__stat-label gh-font-secondary">tested up to six times</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="comprehensive-testing__image-wrap">
      <img
        class="comprehensive-testing__image"
        src="{{ 'standard_shutterstock_2446157489.png' | asset_url }}"
        alt="Petri dishes representing comprehensive testing"
        width="860"
        height="860"
      >
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% comment %} What we test for {% endcomment %}

{{ 'static-WeTestFor-carousel.js' | asset_url | script_tag }}
<section
  class="src static-reviews-carousel"
  {% if block %}
    {{- block.shopify_attributes -}}
  {% endif %}
  style="
                                                                                background: url('{{ ' standard_shutterstock_643406503.png' | asset_url }}') center bottom / cover no-repeat;
  "
>
  <div class="src__inner">
    <h2 class="src__heading gh-font-secondary">What We Test For</h2>

    <div class="src__carousel-outer">
      <div
        class="src__track"
        role="region"
        aria-label="Customer reviews"
        tabindex="0"
      >
        {% comment %} Test Panel 1 {% endcomment %}
        <div class="src__card" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="src__product">Botanical Identification</h3>
          <div class="src__stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="src__text gh-font-secondary">
            Sometimes, we only use a specific part of a plant, like the leaf or root, because it contains the most
            beneficial compounds. If we can’t identify a botanical, or if it contains a part we don’t want, we reject
            the entire batch.
          </p>
          <div class="src__meta gh-font-secondary">
            <strong>Our Methodology:</strong>
            <ul>
              <li>FTIR Spectroscopy</li>
              <li>HPTLC</li>
              <li>Microscopy</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        {% comment %} Test Panel 2 {% endcomment %}
        <div class="src__card" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="src__product">Microbes</h3>
          <div class="src__stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="src__text gh-font-secondary">To ensure your supplements are safe for daily use, we look for:</p>
          <div class="src__meta gh-font-secondary">
            <ul>
              <li>Total Plate Count</li>
              <li>Total Coliform</li>
              <li>Yeast</li>
              <li>Mold</li>
              <li>E. Coli</li>
              <li>Staphylococcus</li>
              <li>Salmonella</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        {% comment %} Test Panel 3 {% endcomment %}
        <div class="src__card" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="src__product">Heavy Metals</h3>
          <div class="src__stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="src__text gh-font-secondary">
            Some heavy metals, like iron and zinc, are essential micronutrients. We test for harmful levels of the “big
            four” toxic heavy metals, plus aluminum:
          </p>
          <div class="src__meta gh-font-secondary">
            <ul>
              <li>Arsenic</li>
              <li>Cadmium</li>
              <li>Lead</li>
              <li>Mercury</li>
              <li>Aluminum</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        {% comment %} Test Panel 4 {% endcomment %}
        <div class="src__card" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="src__product">Adenosine Triphosphate (ATP)</h3>
          <div class="src__stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="src__text gh-font-secondary">
            We test for ATP, a molecule found in all living cells, after cleaning and sanitizing our equipment to ensure
            there is no biological residue from plants or humans. It’s not required, but we do it anyway.
          </p>
        </div>

        {% comment %} Test Panel 5 {% endcomment %}
        <div class="src__card" role="listitem">
          <h3 class="src__product">Potency</h3>
          <div class="src__stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="src__text gh-font-secondary">
            For products with potency listed on the label (like
            <a href="https://globalhealing.com/products/vitamin-d">Vitamin D3</a>), we test the finished product to
            ensure the formula meets our label claim at the time of purchase up to its best-by date.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        class="src__progress"
        aria-hidden="true"
        role="progressbar"
        aria-valuenow="1"
        aria-valuemin="1"
        aria-valuemax="3"
      >
        <div class="src__progress-track">
          <div class="src__progress-fill"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="methodology-cards">
  <div class="methodology-cards__inner">
    <h2 class="methodology-cards__heading gh-font-secondary">Our Methodology</h2>

    <div class="methodology-cards__slider">
      <div class="methodology-cards__track">
        <article class="methodology-cards__item">
          <div class="methodology-cards__media">
            <img
              class="methodology-cards__image"
              src="{{ 'Standard_Testing_Standards_Page_FTIR_Spectroscopy.jpg' | asset_url }}"
              alt="FTIR Spectroscopy"
              width="800"
              height="440"
            >
          </div>
          <div class="methodology-cards__content">
            <h3 class="methodology-cards__title">FTIR Spectroscopy</h3>
            <p class="methodology-cards__text gh-font-secondary">
              Using an infrared light, we scan an ingredient’s unique “fingerprint” to confirm a raw ingredient is what
              it’s supposed to be.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="methodology-cards__item">
          <div class="methodology-cards__media">
            <img
              class="methodology-cards__image"
              src="{{ 'standard_Testing-Standards-Page_HPTLC.jpg' | asset_url }}"
              alt="HPTLC"
              width="800"
              height="440"
            >
          </div>
          <div class="methodology-cards__content">
            <h3 class="methodology-cards__title">HPTLC</h3>
            <p class="methodology-cards__text gh-font-secondary">
              We separate a plant’s compounds and compare them to a pre‑verified reference, allowing us to rule out
              adulterants or fillers.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="methodology-cards__item">
          <div class="methodology-cards__media">
            <img
              class="methodology-cards__image"
              src="{{ 'standard_Testing_Standards_Page_Microscopy.jpg' | asset_url }}"
              alt="Microscopy"
              width="800"
              height="440"
            >
          </div>
          <div class="methodology-cards__content">
            <h3 class="methodology-cards__title">Microscopy</h3>
            <p class="methodology-cards__text gh-font-secondary">
              Using a microscope, we verify characteristics that cannot be identified by chemical analysis, such as
              cellular structure.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="methodology-cards__progress" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="methodology-cards__progress-track">
        <div class="methodology-cards__progress-fill"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="methodology-cards__cta">
      <button type="button" class="methodology-cards__popup-trigger gh-font-secondary">
        See the Complete Testing Process
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="methodology-cards-popup" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="methodology-cards-popup__dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Complete testing process">
    <button type="button" class="methodology-cards-popup__close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <img
      class="methodology-cards-popup__image"
      src="{{ 'Standard_Complete_Testing_Process_Chart.jpg' | asset_url }}"
      alt="Diagram showing the complete testing process"
      width="100%"
      height="100%"
    >
  </div>
</div>

